Z||000002||Daleford||12-06-2000||08:01 AM||||Yes, 200 horses from a V-6 might be OK, but I crave that V-8 sound.  Guess the only Ford FWD V-8 unit was the 95-up Continental 4.6.<BR>Trouble is, all its electronics scare me. I have heard you would even have to use the complete dash cluster to make it work right! <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||12-06-2000||11:26 AM||||You want some real fun, put Pontiac back into it! I've heard of someone working out an old Pontiac engine under the deck lid. Prior to '77 Pontiac made their own engines (non-GM style) I think the guy was running a 400ci, but imagine an old 450 with a 6 pack, torque from heck coming out of those power plants. <P>Pnacho Power!!||||reg||1
