Z||000005||Got2manyfieros||12-06-2000||02:40 PM||||There was a guy named Gary Zumalt that used to do fiero V8 conversions like Archie, but he used the pontiac V8..this causes some issues because the pontiac motor is something like 3 inches longer, and requires custom axle shafts, and the whole deal has to be moved towards the driver's side.  I believe that kit is no longer available though...||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||12-06-2000||05:02 PM||||What about Toyota engines? Toyota makes some of the best engines like the v8 that is in my Tundra. It is a 4.7-liter 32 valve double overhead cam engine with gobs of low end torque and 245 horsepower. It is as fast or faster than the optional v8's in the domestic pickup trucks. Plus Toyota engines are reliable.||||reg||1
