Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||12-06-2000||08:02 PM||||My mom's car has a ford 3.8L V6, but the Fiero has better acceleration.. torque is probably about the same, though I've never compared the numbers.<P>my mom's started to complain about the car, so I asked her if she'd let me do some mods to it when I'm home for the summer.. first thing she wants is brighter headlights.. no problem. I'm also going to put in a K&N filter, to improve top end performance a bit.. it's not a sports car AT ALL, but it could still use some improvement.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'll save the REAL mods for my Fiero..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000012||JohnnyK||12-06-2000||08:32 PM||||Man, be real. The K&N isn't going to do a thing in that car (sorry to burst your bubble.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">... As for other engines, I'm sure if you had access to some simple machines, anything would be fairly easy. Motor mounts aren't that hard I'm assuming. From what I saw in my duke anyways.||||reg||1
Z||000013||william_thorniii||12-06-2000||08:39 PM||||JonnyK,<P>What do you mean that a K&N "will do nothing" for that car?  <P>Fact is that K&N's typically help out cars not optimized from the factory (like a Taurus) more than they will help a car that has been optimized from the factory (like a Fiero).  In fact the majority of the "performance gains" that those type of products site bank on you replacing an extremely restrictive airbox, inlet tube, etc.  That is specifically HOW they increase power, but providing a better path for the air to follow.  The filters are not that revolutionary.  <P>Have you seen any dyno tests (with your own eyes) that will disprove me?  If so please draw them to my attention.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
